{"subtitle": "a novella", "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "Two friends, two sons, two shocking and intense love affairs...  Roz and Lil have been best friends since childhood. But their bond stretches beyond familiar bounds when these middle-aged mothers fall in love with each other's teenage sons--taboo-shattering passions that last for years, until the women end them, vowing to have a respectable old age. With Adore, Doris Lessing, winner of the Nobel Prize for Literature, once again proves her unrivaled ability to capture the truth of the human condition."}, "isbn_10": ["0062318969"], "local_id": ["urn:sfpl:31223103956919", "urn:sfpl:31223103956810", "urn:sfpl:31223103956869", "urn:sfpl:31223103956877", "urn:sfpl:31223103956927", "urn:sfpl:31223103956844", "urn:sfpl:31223103956828", "urn:sfpl:31223103956984", "urn:sfpl:31223103956976", "urn:sfpl:31223103956968", "urn:bwbsku:W3-ADS-429"], "full_title": "Adore a novella", "lc_classifications": ["PR6023.E833 A86 2013"], "key": "/books/OL27155231M", "authors": [{"key": "/authors/OL27709A"}], "isbn_13": ["9780062318961"], "pagination": "70, 29 pages", "source_records": ["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run04.mrc:395429874:4044", "bwb:9780062318961", "amazon:0062318969", "ia:adorenovella0000less", "promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17", "marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.13.20150123.full.mrc:867691575:1684", "marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_014.bib.mrc:344388732:2516"], "title": "Adore", "work_titles": ["Novels"], "notes": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "\"Originally published as \"The Grandmothers\" in the collection The Grandmothers: Four Short Novels in hardcover in the United States in 2004 by HarperCollins Publishers.\"--Title page verso."}, "number_of_pages": 70, "languages": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "dewey_decimal_class": ["823/.914"], "subjects": ["Man-woman relationships", "English Short stories", "Fiction"], "publish_date": "2013"